From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H. M. Yousuf <hmyousuf@nirapod.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:21:57 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] tests: expected outputs of the combined series

The expected outputs of the negative and safety test suites are generated
by their runners. The patches of the series were written on different
bases, and each records the output of its own base. On the combined tree
the outputs differ in three generated parts only: the asmgen messages of
the Advanced SIMD negative tests now use upstream's message format, with
the address forms of a 128-bit load or store; the negative test count
and the order of the RISC-V entries follow from the tests the series
adds; and the safety report of the shift-bound tests lists the ARMv8-A
runs, which the ARMv8-A checker adds, with its relational constraints in
sorted order. No verdict changes.
---
